{
  "kanji": "帰",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 帰\ntitle: return home\njlpt: 4\ntags: [jlpt-n4, grade-2, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 10\nradical: 巾\nradicalNumber: 50\nonyomi: [キ]\nkunyomi: [かえ.る, かえ.す, おく.る, とつ.ぐ]\ndistractors: [書, 建, 用]\n---\n\n# 帰 — return home\n\n**Strokes:** 10 · **Key (radical):** 巾 (no. 50) · **JLPT:** N4 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n帰 concerns returning home or to a place one belongs. In [帰る](../words/帰る.md), it can be translated as either \"go home\" or \"come home,\" depending on the viewpoint.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the short strokes on the left as a traveler approaching the layered doorway on the right, with 巾 hanging below. This is a memory story, not a historical analysis.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe table is selective; metadata also preserves おく.る and とつ.ぐ.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| キ | on | 帰国 きこく — return to one's country |\n| かえ.る | kun | [帰る](../words/帰る.md) かえる — go or come home |\n| かえ.す | kun | 帰す かえす — send someone home |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [帰る](../words/帰る.md) かえる — return home\n- 帰り かえり — return, way back\n- 帰国 きこく — return to one's country\n- 帰す かえす — send someone home\n\n## Notes\n\n[行](行.md) in 行く いく describes going; [来](来.md) in 来る くる describes coming. 帰る adds the idea of returning to a home or base, not just motion in either direction.\n\nDespite ending in える, 帰る is a godan verb: 帰ります かえります, 帰って かえって. Keep the classical radical 巾 distinct from the other visible parts of the character.\n\nFor 帰る compared with 返る, 還る, and the differently conjugated change/replacement verbs, see [Kaeru: change, replace, exchange, and return](../articles/kaeru-change-replace-and-return.md).\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-281; James William Breen and EDRDG ([CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/)).\n",
